config BR2_PACKAGE_OPENIMP
	bool
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_ISP_OPEN
	depends on BR2_THINGINO_DEV_CAMERA
	select BR2_PACKAGE_TINYALSA if BR2_SOC_FAMILY = "t31" && KERNEL_VERSION_7
	help
	  OpenIMP is an open-source implementation of the Ingenic IMP
	  (Image Media Process) library. It provides a
	  reverse-engineered implementation of libimp.so that can
	  replace the proprietary Ingenic library.

	  Current upstream builds support T20, T21, T23, T30, T31, T40,
	  and T41. This package installs the matching build/<soc>/libimp.so
	  in staging and on the target, then preserves that replacement
	  during target finalization.

	  T30 is video-only: its build deliberately refuses to export the
	  IMP audio entry points. T20/T21 reuse the T31 audio implementation;
	  T31/T40/T41 export the IMP_AI/IMP_AO capture and playback paths.
	  The audio-capable builds also export IMP_AENC/IMP_ADEC and the
	  encoder fisheye controls, so prudynt links against OpenIMP. Some
	  optional OSD/IVS entry points remain incomplete.

	  https://github.com/opensensor/openimp
